a bitmap face is never a fallback

FcFontMatch NEVER FAILS, it substitutes, and FC_OUTLINE on the pattern is only a PREFERENCE. For a
character that nothing installed covers with an outline face, fontconfig hands back Noto Color
Emoji: it answers scalable, it really does have the character, and it is a CBDT bitmap font. This
renderer needs an outline to scale, so taking it printed

  FreeType font face is not scalable: family=Noto Color Emoji style=Regular glyphs=4027

and Money Manager EX ABORTED, 3 runs in 3, with no window ever drawn.

So the match is now CHECKED as well as preferred: FcPatternGetBool of FC_OUTLINE on the RESULT, next
to the FcCharSetHasChar check that was already there for the same reason. Preferring a property and
requiring it are not the same question when the matcher cannot fail.

Found while building the layout half of the font fallback, which is NOT in this patch and is
recorded in #216: it regressed mmex on its own and was reverted.
--- a/Onyx2D/O2Font_freetype.m
+++ b/Onyx2D/O2Font_freetype.m
@@ -224,6 +224,11 @@
 
         FcPatternAddCharSet(pattern, FC_CHARSET, charset);
         FcPatternAddBool(pattern, FC_SCALABLE, FcTrue);
+        /* OUTLINE AS WELL AS SCALABLE, because they are not the same question and the difference
+         * killed mmex outright. Noto Color Emoji answers scalable, covers half the symbol range,
+         * and is a BITMAP face: the renderer here needs an outline to scale, said "FreeType font
+         * face is not scalable" and the process aborted. */
+        FcPatternAddBool(pattern, FC_OUTLINE, FcTrue);
         FcConfigSubstitute(config, pattern, FcMatchPattern);
         FcDefaultSubstitute(pattern);
 
@@ -234,8 +239,15 @@
              * character is the normal answer for a script nothing installed covers. Returning it
              * would swap the face and still draw nothing. */
             FcCharSet *covered = NULL;
+            FcBool outline = FcFalse;
 
-            if (FcPatternGetCharSet(match, FC_CHARSET, 0, &covered) == FcResultMatch &&
+            /* CHECK THE MATCH, do not merely prefer. FC_OUTLINE on the pattern is a preference and
+             * fontconfig never fails: for a character only a colour emoji face covers it hands that
+             * back anyway. This renderer needs an outline to scale, and taking a bitmap face made
+             * mmex print "FreeType font face is not scalable" and abort. */
+            if (FcPatternGetBool(match, FC_OUTLINE, 0, &outline) == FcResultMatch &&
+                outline == FcTrue &&
+                FcPatternGetCharSet(match, FC_CHARSET, 0, &covered) == FcResultMatch &&
                 covered != NULL && FcCharSetHasChar(covered, code)) {
                 FcChar8 *unparsed = FcNameUnparse(match);
 
